      "message": "Preliminarily, `cap-\u003ecoalesce_on_map` sounds reasonable.\n\nThough we might also add a TODO to remove it in the future, once we implement TLB flush for hyp_mmu (which we want in order to be able to unmap unused mappings as needed - b/541580341), so that we have no particular reason to avoid coalescing for hyp_mmu anymore.\n\nHmm... then maybe just remove that BUG() instead, making `hyp_mmu_flush_tlb()` a successful no-op for now (with a comment explaining why exactly it is so)?",
